---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegacyHeader from '../components/LegacyHeader.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactSection from '../components/ContactSection.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ButtonPrimary from '../components/ButtonPrimary.astro';
import ButtonSecondary from '../components/ButtonSecondary.astro';
import { seoServicesHreflangs } from '../data/internationalSeoPages.js';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How much do SEO services cost per month in the United States?',
    answer: "US agency retainers typically run $2,500 to $10,000 per month, with most small businesses paying $1,500 to $5,000 and competitive verticals like legal and finance reaching $10,000 to $50,000+. Hourly rates typically sit between $100 and $250. Because our senior team works from the Philippines, the same hours of qualified work cost meaningfully less. We scope every campaign in USD against your actual competitors and quote in writing before you commit — no surprise line items."
  },
  {
    question: 'Is cheap $99-per-month SEO safe?',
    answer: "Usually not. At US rates, $99 buys well under an hour of qualified work, so those shops lean on automation, spun content and spammy link networks — tactics that can trigger penalties costing far more to undo than real SEO would have cost in the first place. Offshore delivery lowers the price of legitimate hours; it does not make one hour do the work of twenty. If a price only makes sense with shortcuts, shortcuts are what you are buying."
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does SEO take to show results?',
    answer: "Plan for meaningful movement in three to six months and compounding gains after that. Our published case studies reflect that honestly: a bridal ecommerce brand grew organic clicks 137.5% over a three-month comparison, while a pest control firm needed a six-month window to recover from a Google core update with a 128% click increase. Anyone promising page one in 30 days is describing either luck or spam."
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you guarantee #1 rankings on Google?',
    answer: "No — and no honest agency can. Rankings are decided by algorithms nobody outside Google controls, so a guaranteed-#1 pitch is a sales tactic, not a service. What we do instead: agree realistic targets up front, publish our results honestly — several of our case studies show metrics that dipped alongside the ones that grew — and report monthly against the numbers that matter: clicks, conversions and revenue."
  },
  {
    question: 'What is included in your monthly SEO services?',
    answer: "A defined monthly scope built from six workstreams: technical SEO, on-page optimization, content production in American English, US-relevant link building, keyword and competitor research, and AI search optimization. Each month you receive completed deliverables — pages shipped, fixes deployed, links earned — not activity summaries, plus a report tied to Google Analytics 4 and Search Console data you can verify yourself."
  },
  {
    question: 'Who actually does the SEO work?',
    answer: "The in-house team in Quezon City that we name publicly: founder Ben Lowe, who brings over 15 years of SEO experience, co-founder Sassin Lowe, SEO manager Janin A. Cañonero and SEO expert Jewe O. Manalo. Nothing is passed to anonymous subcontractors, and senior review happens on everything we ship. Ask any US agency quoting $5,000 a month the same question — the answer is often much less direct."
  },
  {
    question: 'How do you measure and report SEO results?',
    answer: "Monthly reports built on Google Analytics 4, Google Search Console and SE Ranking — the same sources every published Bright Forge case study cites — plus live dashboard access through our SEO Command Centre, so you can check progress any day rather than waiting for report day. You keep ownership of your analytics properties; if you ever leave, your data and access leave with you."
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you require long-term contracts, and how does billing work?',
    answer: "We invoice in US dollars by default and accept international bank transfer and card payments. Scope, deliverables and terms are agreed in writing before any money changes hands, and we aim to earn renewals with results rather than lock-ins. Our published Google reviews include a UK auctions platform that has worked with us for over 18 months and another client of about three years — retention we earned month by month."
  },
  {
    question: 'How do the time zones between the US and the Philippines work?',
    answer: "Manila is 12 to 13 hours ahead of US Eastern time and 15 to 16 ahead of Pacific, which turns the difference into an overnight turnaround: brief us before you log off, and finished work is waiting when you start your next day. For calls, our morning overlaps with US evenings and our evening with US mornings — we schedule around your calendar, not ours."
  },
  {
    question: 'Will my content be written in American English?',
    answer: "Yes. US campaigns get American spelling and terminology — optimization, color, analyze — plus US buyer language, US units and US cultural references, with human editorial review before anything is delivered. No British spelling on your landing pages, no raw AI dumps published under your brand. It is a small detail that quietly signals to both Google and your customers that the page was written for them."
  },
  {
    question: 'How do AI Overviews and ChatGPT search change SEO?',
    answer: "Materially — and measurably. For a leather goods ecommerce client we grew LLM referral sessions 434.7% over a six-month comparison (August 2025 to January 2026), with ChatGPT driving 93% of that AI traffic and visitors arriving from 75 countries. The work overlaps heavily with classic SEO — entity clarity, answer-ready structure, strong product pages — which is why we build AI search optimization into US campaigns rather than selling it as an upsell."
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you do local SEO for US cities?',
    answer: "Yes. We optimize Google Business Profiles, local landing pages, citations and review strategy for US businesses with physical locations or service areas. One honest caveat: map-pack visibility depends on your real US location and proximity — no agency anywhere can fake that. The organic side — local pages, content, links — can be executed from anywhere, and that is exactly what we do."
  }
];

const schema = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Service',
      name: 'SEO Services USA',
      serviceType: 'Search engine optimization',
      description:
        'Senior SEO services for United States businesses: technical SEO, American-English content, US-relevant link building, local SEO and AI search optimization, delivered overnight from the Philippines.',
      url: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/seo-services-usa/',
      areaServed: { '@type': 'Country', name: 'United States' },
      provider: {
        '@type': 'Organization',
        name: 'Bright Forge SEO',
        url: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/'
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'SEO Services USA', item: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/seo-services-usa/' }
      ]
    }
  ]
});
---

<MainLayout
  title="SEO Services USA | Senior SEO Team at Offshore Rates"
  description="SEO services for US businesses from a senior Philippines team. Real case-study results, American-English content, US links — brief at 5pm ET, done by 8am."
  canonical="https://brightforge.com.ph/seo-services-usa/"
  type="service"
  faqs={faqs}
  hreflangs={seoServicesHreflangs}
  geoRegion="US"
  geoPlacename="United States"
  contentLanguage="en-US"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={schema} />

  <LegacyHeader slot="header" />

  <Hero
    badgeIcon="fas fa-globe-americas"
    badgeText="SEO for US Businesses"
    title="SEO Services USA: <span>Senior SEO Done While You Sleep</span>"
    breadcrumbCurrent="SEO Services USA"
  >
    <Fragment slot="story">
      <p>Bright Forge SEO helps US ecommerce brands, SaaS companies and service businesses compete on google.com with senior technical SEO, American-English content, US-relevant link building and reporting that answers the only question that matters: is this making us money?</p>
      <p>We are based in the Philippines, which gives US clients two structural advantages: your budget buys execution instead of agency overhead, and the 12-hour time difference means you brief us at the end of your day and finished work is in your inbox the next morning.</p>
      <p>The proof is published, not promised: case studies with real Search Console numbers — including a 137.5% organic click increase in three months — and a 5.0 rating on Google from 12 reviews.</p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <ButtonPrimary href="/contact/" text="Get a US SEO Proposal" />
      <ButtonSecondary href="#results" text="See Real Results" />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <div class="market-visual" aria-label="US SEO campaign snapshot">
        <div class="market-node">
          <span>Your market</span>
          <strong>google.com, US buyers, US competitors</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="market-line"></div>
        <div class="market-node forge">
          <span>Your SEO team</span>
          <strong>Senior delivery from the Philippines</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="market-line"></div>
        <div class="market-node">
          <span>Your advantage</span>
          <strong>Brief today, deliverables tomorrow morning</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <section class="proof-strip" aria-label="US SEO proof points">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="proof-grid">
        <div><strong>+137.5% organic clicks</strong><span>Bridal ecommerce, 3-month comparison</span></div>
        <div><strong>5.0 on Google</strong><span>12 five-star reviews</span></div>
        <div><strong>15+ years of expertise</strong><span>Founder-led senior review on all work</span></div>
        <div><strong>Overnight turnaround</strong><span>Your night is our workday</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Proof, not promises</p>
        <h2>Results from <span>published, honest case studies</span></h2>
        <p>Every number below comes from a published case study built on Google Analytics 4, Search Console and SE Ranking data. Our clients compete in Western, English-language search results — the same algorithms, the same SERP features, the same fight you face on google.com. We label results honestly, including the metrics that dipped.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="results-grid">
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-stat">+137.5%</p>
          <h3>Bridal fashion ecommerce</h3>
          <p>Organic clicks grew from 7.4k to 17.6k over a three-month comparison, with average position climbing from 24.8 to 14.9 — a ten-place lift the case study itself is careful to note is not yet a first-page claim.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/bridal-dress-designer-seo/">Read the case study</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-stat">+128%</p>
          <h3>Pest control — core update recovery</h3>
          <p>After a Google core update knocked this local services firm down, a six-month recovery campaign took organic clicks from 10.3k to 23.5k while impressions grew 147%.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/pest-control-core-update-seo/">Read the case study</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-stat">+34%</p>
          <h3>Football app — 68k extra clicks</h3>
          <p>Organic clicks rose from 200k to 268k over a three-month comparison, with average position improving from 11.4 to 9.1 — into page-one territory for a high-volume sports platform.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/football-app-seo/">Read the case study</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-stat">+49.3%</p>
          <h3>DTC leather goods ecommerce</h3>
          <p>Organic clicks grew from 15.2k to 22.7k while click-through rate jumped from 3.1% to 4.5% — better rankings and better snippets for a direct-to-consumer brand.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/leather-wallet-ecommerce-seo/">Read the case study</a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="geo-banner">
        <p class="result-stat">+434.7%</p>
        <div>
          <h3>AI search is already sending buyers</h3>
          <p>For a leather goods ecommerce brand we grew LLM referral sessions 434.7% over six months (August 2025 to January 2026) — 93% of that traffic from ChatGPT, with visitors from 75 countries and product pages earning 5 to 10x more AI referrals than category pages. <a href="/case-studies/ai-leather-goods-ecommerce-geo/">See the AI search case study</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="honesty-note">We publish the declines too. Our <a href="/case-studies/car-auction-seo/">car auction case study</a> shows average position and CTR falling even as impressions grew 32% and clicks 5% — because that is what the data said. If an agency's case studies contain no bad numbers, ask what they are hiding.</p>

      <div class="testimonial-grid">
        <blockquote class="quote-card">
          <p>&ldquo;Bright Forge SEO delivered exceptional results for our fitness equipment brand... The consistent uptick in engagement has reinforced our brand credibility in the competitive fitness market.&rdquo;</p>
          <footer>Luke, Marketing Director, Speediance UK</footer>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote-card">
          <p>&ldquo;We've been working with Ben and Bright Forge SEO for over 18 months, with the primary focus being our SEO needs. They deliver excellent results.&rdquo;</p>
          <footer>UK Auction List</footer>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote-card">
          <p>&ldquo;We're seeing more qualified leads coming through our website, and our consultants are spending less time prospecting and more time delivering value to clients.&rdquo;</p>
          <footer>Sarah Thompson, Marketing Director, Professional Consulting Firm</footer>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote-card">
          <p>&ldquo;We've been working with Bright Forge SEO for about three years now and they've been great. Really solid all-round SEO.&rdquo;</p>
          <footer>Louise Maclean</footer>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="why-us">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why US businesses choose this SEO agency</p>
        <h2>The most competitive market needs <span>budget spent on work, not overhead</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">Competing on google.com means out-executing well-funded rivals. Every dollar that goes to a US agency's office lease and account-management layers is a dollar not spent on content, fixes and links.</p>
        <p>The Philippines has been the outsourcing partner of choice for US companies for decades for a reason: English is an official language, the working culture is US-aligned, and senior talent costs a fraction of coastal-agency rates. We put that arbitrage to work on your rankings — same hours, same seniority, more of your budget doing actual SEO.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid small">
        <article class="card"><h3>Ecommerce brands</h3><p>Category and product page SEO plus content that captures US buying intent against marketplace giants.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>SaaS and platforms</h3><p>Comparison, feature and use-case pages plus authority building for brutal US software SERPs.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Service businesses</h3><p>Service and location page strategy, Google Business Profile work and local organic visibility for US cities.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>US agencies</h3><p>White label SEO fulfillment under your brand — see our <a href="/white-label-seo-services-philippines/">white label SEO services</a> for the overnight partnership model.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="services">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we deliver</p>
        <h2>Full-service <span>SEO for the US market</span></h2>
        <p>Every campaign is built around your market, your competitors and your commercial goals — not a fixed task list. These are the workstreams we draw on.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="service-grid">
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-search"></i><h3>SEO audits</h3><p>Technical, content and authority diagnosis against your real US competitors, with prioritized fixes. See our <a href="/seo-audit-services/">SEO audit services</a>.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-sitemap"></i><h3>Technical SEO</h3><p>Crawlability, indexation, site speed, schema and structure — the <a href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">technical SEO</a> foundations US rankings are built on.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-pen-nib"></i><h3>US content SEO</h3><p>American-English <a href="/content-seo-services-philippines/">content SEO</a> mapped to US search demand, buyer language and commercial intent.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-link"></i><h3>US link building</h3><p>Relevance-led <a href="/backlink-seo-services-philippines/">link building</a> from American publications, directories and industry sites. No spam packages.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-key"></i><h3>Keyword research</h3><p>US search demand mapped to pages through <a href="/keyword-research-services/">keyword research</a> sized honestly against the competition you actually face.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-robot"></i><h3>AI Search Optimization</h3><p>Entity clarity and answer-ready structure via <a href="/ai-search-optimization-services-philippines/">AI search optimization</a>, so US buyers find you in ChatGPT and AI Overviews.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-map-marker-alt"></i><h3>US local SEO</h3><p>Google Business Profile, local pages, citations and reviews — <a href="/local-seo-services-philippines/">local SEO services</a> for location-based US businesses.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-truck-moving"></i><h3>Website migrations</h3><p>Replatforming or redesigning? Our <a href="/website-migration-services/">website migration services</a> protect the rankings you already own.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="services-note">Running a US agency? The same team handles white label fulfillment overnight, under your brand, with client-ready reporting.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="process">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">How campaigns run</p>
        <h2>Your first 90 days, <span>delivered overnight</span></h2>
        <p>The overnight cycle is not a slogan — it is the delivery schedule. Everything below lands in your inbox by your morning, and we are still online for questions when you read it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="process-grid">
        <article class="month-card">
          <span class="month-tag">Month 1</span>
          <h3>Diagnose and fix</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Full technical, content and authority audit against named US competitors</li>
            <li>Keyword and competitor-gap research mapped to specific pages</li>
            <li>Prioritized roadmap agreed with you by week two</li>
            <li>Highest-impact technical fixes start shipping immediately</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="month-card">
          <span class="month-tag">Month 2</span>
          <h3>Build</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>On-page optimization rolled out across priority pages</li>
            <li>First batch of American-English content drafted, reviewed and published</li>
            <li>US link prospecting and outreach begins</li>
            <li>Google Business Profile and local pages for location-based businesses</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="month-card">
          <span class="month-tag">Month 3</span>
          <h3>Compound</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Link placements land; content velocity holds steady</li>
            <li>First full performance review against your baseline</li>
            <li>Strategy adjusted by data, not by gut feel</li>
            <li>Clear next-quarter targets in writing</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="process-note">From day one you get monthly reporting plus live dashboard access through our <a href="/seo-command-centre/">SEO Command Centre</a> — GA4, Search Console and SE Ranking data you can check any day, not just report day.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="pricing">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing, honestly</p>
        <h2>What SEO services typically cost <span>in the United States</span></h2>
        <p>Comprehensive US agency retainers typically run $2,500 to $10,000 per month. Most small businesses pay $1,500 to $5,000, local campaigns cluster around $400 to $1,500, and competitive verticals like legal, finance and SaaS reach $10,000 to $50,000+. Hourly rates typically range from $100 to $250.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <article class="price-card avoid">
          <h3>$99 &ldquo;page one guaranteed&rdquo; shops</h3>
          <p class="price-tag">Avoid</p>
          <p>At US rates, $99 buys under an hour of qualified work. These shops survive on automation, spun content and spammy link networks — and their penalties become your cleanup bill.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="price-card">
          <h3>Typical US agency retainer</h3>
          <p class="price-tag">$2,500&ndash;$10,000/mo</p>
          <p>Often genuinely senior strategy — but a large share of the retainer pays for account-management layers, downtown offices and US salary costs, not hands-on optimization of your site.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="price-card featured">
          <h3>The Bright Forge model</h3>
          <p class="price-tag">Scoped in USD, quoted up front</p>
          <p>Same senior hours at a Philippine cost structure, so the budget goes into execution: fixes shipped, content published, links earned. Scope and terms in writing before you commit.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="pricing-note">The hour math is what matters. Real SEO on a competitive US site typically needs 15 to 40 hours a month; industry pricing guides warn that anything under $500 a month buys two to three US-rate hours at best. &ldquo;Affordable&rdquo; done right does not mean fewer hours — it means the same hours at a lower cost base. That is the entire offshore case, and it is also why we will never publish a one-size package price: your competitors set the workload, so we scope against them and quote accordingly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="choose">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Buyer's guide</p>
        <h2>How to choose an <span>SEO company in the United States</span></h2>
        <p>Whether you hire a Manhattan agency, a freelancer or an offshore team like ours, the vetting questions are identical. Here is the checklist we would use — and how we answer it ourselves.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="choose-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Ask who does the work</h3><p>Many agencies sell senior strategy and deliver junior or subcontracted execution. Demand names. Ours are public: the team below, in-house in Quezon City.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Demand dated, sourced metrics</h3><p>Case studies should cite tools (GA4, Search Console) and timeframes — and include numbers that went the wrong way. Perfect-looking portfolios are curated, not honest.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Treat guarantees as a red flag</h3><p>Nobody controls Google. &ldquo;Guaranteed #1&rdquo; means spam tactics, cherry-picked zero-volume keywords, or both.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Keep your own analytics access</h3><p>You should own your GA4, Search Console and Business Profile. If an agency insists on owning them, they are building a hostage situation, not a campaign.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Do the hour math on the price</h3><p>Divide the retainer by a realistic hourly rate for the team's location. If the hours cannot cover the promises, the promises are the product.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Check retention, not just wins</h3><p>Clients who stay are the strongest signal. Our published reviews include an auctions platform at 18+ months and a client of about three years.</p></article>
      </div>

      <div class="team-strip">
        <div>
          <h3>The people behind the work</h3>
          <p>Bright Forge SEO was founded by Ben Lowe — over 15 years in SEO, a marketing degree from Metro London University and industry certifications — alongside co-founder Sassin Lowe. Campaigns are run by SEO manager Janin A. Cañonero and SEO expert Jewe O. Manalo, with senior review on everything that ships. Meet the full team on our <a href="/about-us/">about page</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="team-names">
          <span>Ben Lowe<em>CEO &amp; Co-Founder</em></span>
          <span>Sassin Lowe<em>CEO &amp; Co-Founder</em></span>
          <span>Janin A. Cañonero<em>SEO Manager</em></span>
          <span>Jewe O. Manalo<em>SEO Expert</em></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="timezone">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The practical stuff</p>
        <h2>The 12-hour difference is <span>a delivery superpower</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">Manila is roughly 12 hours ahead of New York and 15 ahead of Los Angeles. Our entire workday fits inside your night.</p>
        <p>Send requirements at 5pm Eastern and we are just starting our day. By your next morning the audit is done, the fixes are documented, the content is drafted. US agencies charge rush rates for that turnaround; for us it is just the clock. And because our morning overlaps your evening (and vice versa), same-day calls are never a problem.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timezone-card">
        <h3>A typical working day</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>5:00pm ET / 5:00am PH</strong> — you send briefs and feedback before logging off</li>
          <li><strong>Your overnight</strong> — audits, fixes, content and reporting completed during our business hours</li>
          <li><strong>8:00am ET / 8:00pm PH</strong> — deliverables in your inbox; we are still online for questions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="industries">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Industries served</p>
        <h2>US verticals we know <span>from the inside</span></h2>
        <p>Our published case-study portfolio spans ecommerce, SaaS, consulting, local services and sports platforms. For these US-heavy industries we maintain dedicated playbooks.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="industry-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/real-estate-seo-services/">Real estate</a></h3><p>Agent, brokerage and listings-site SEO for hyper-local, high-value US searches.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/home-services-seo/">Home services</a></h3><p>HVAC, plumbing, roofing and pest control — our core update recovery case was a pest control firm.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/finance-crypto-seo-services/">Finance &amp; crypto</a></h3><p>Finance pages live or die on trust. We keep claims holdable and build authority the same way the rest of the campaign is built.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3><a href="/gaming-seo-services/">Gaming</a></h3><p>Publisher, platform and community SEO in fast-moving, high-volume entertainment SERPs.</p></article>
